test_smAgent: 430 passed, 0 failed (the ❌ lines are expected console.error output from negative-path tests). Threads 10, 13 done. Now thread 11 (I5 wiring). Implement `silentUpdateBranchTracked` + `recordSilentUpdateFailure` in smAgent.

Design:
```js
// gh-100 I5 — silent-update clone-failure bookkeeping: post the failure
// marker (attempt N at ISO), and at 0 attempts left flag the PR
// 'silent-update-degraded' (visible state instead of silent eternal retry).
function recordSilentUpdateFailure(key, ticket) { ... }
```

Where to place: near silentUpdateBranch definition (inside processRule scope? silentUpdateBranch is defined inside processRule — a nested function). recordSilentUpdateFailure needs: effectiveRepoInfo, githubTracker, validationLivenessModule, github_get_pr_comments — all available in processRule scope. I'll define it next to silentUpdateBranch inside processRule, and wrap both call sites.

Implementation:
```js
function recordSilentUpdateFailure(key, ticket) {
   try {
       var tracker = githubTracker(effectiveRepoInfo.owner, effectiveRepoInfo.repo);
       var comments = tracker.getComments(ticket.prNumber) || [];
       var count = validationLivenessModule.silentUpdateFailureCount(coments);
       var attempt = count.count + 1;
       var iso = new Date().toISOString();
       var left = validationLivenessModule.silentUpdateAttemptsLeft(attempt);
       if (left > 0) {
           tracker.postComment(ticket.prNumber,
               validationLivenessModule.silentUpdateFailureLine(attempt, iso));
           console.warn(' ⚠️ ' + key + ' silent-update failure #' + attempt +
               ' recorded — ' + left + ' attempt(s) left before degraded flag (I5)');
           return;
       }
       // attempts exhausted — flag the PR once (visible state); marker
       // already at MAX, no comment spam beyond it.
       if ((ticket.labels || []).indexOf(validationLivenessModule.SILENT_UPDATE_DEGRADED_LABEL) === -1) {
           tracker.addLabel(ticket.prNumber, validationLivenessModule.SILENT_UPDATE_DEGRADED_LABEL);
       }
       console.error(' ❌ ' + key + ' silent-update degraded after ' +
           validationLivenessModule.SILENT_UPDATE_MAX_FAILURES +
           ' consecutive clone failures — flagged silent-update-degraded (I5)');
   } catch (eI5) {
       console.warn(' ⚠️ ' + key + ' I5 failure bookkeeping failed: ' + (eI5.message || eI5));
   }
```

Check tracker API: getComments(key) exists for github tracker (githubGetComments). addLabel exists. postComment exists.

Wait — the degraded label: once attempts are exhausted, later ticks: count stays 3 → attempt = 4 → left = 0 → label already present (check ticket.labels — the item's labels come from the query; after labeling, next tick's item may carry the label if the query returns it... update_branch rules query BEHIND PRs; labels on the item come from the source query — yes labels flow). But in the same tick the label was just added, ticket.labels doesn't include it. Guard with a fetch? Simpler: check comments? No — keep it idempotent-ish: addLabel may throw if duplicate? Safer: read PR comments only for count; for the label, check ticket.labels AND posted-this-tick flag. Since addLabel duplicate via REST add labels endpoint is idempotent (GitHub add labels to issue that already has them = 200 OK, no dup). gh add labels is idempotent. Fine.

Also wrap the two silentUpdateBranch call sites:

```js
function silentUpdateBranchTracked(branchName) {
   try {
       silentUpdateBranch(branchName);
   } catch (eClone) {
       recordSilentUpdateFailure(key, ticket);
